  "root_cause_classification": {
    "classification": "C. P3 contains a contextual imbalance specifically affecting chases.",
    "primary_justification": "The root cause is a fundamental structural unit asymmetry between 1st and 2nd innings P3. 1st innings P3 uses delta EFS (projected 20-over runs improvement, divisor = 12.0 runs), which scales outward and awards massive scores (+43.4 runs -> 1.81 raw points in Case B). 2nd innings P3 uses delta RRR (runs per over relief, divisor = 3.0 RPO), which is mathematically bounded by the entry RRR (6.36 RPO in Case A). Even liquidating 56% of the target yielded only 2.48 RPO relief (0.41 raw points in Case A). This structural disparity creates a ~16-point deficit in P3 across the entire historical population of explosive powerplay openers.",
    "secondary_ui_bug_identified": "In app/services/data_service.py lines 498-503, the UI signal label inverts the sign of required_rr_change. Because required_rr_change is defined as RRR_entry - RRR_exit (positive = relief), the UI erroneously displayed 'Chase pressure intensified: RRR increased by 2.48 RPO' when RRR had in fact DECREASED by 2.48 RPO. This inverted UI label severely distorted user perception.",
    "compounding_p1_interaction": "The low chase target (128) penalized Case A twice: first inside P3 by capping RRR relief, and second inside P1 by assigning low context difficulty (C_eff = 34.9, Leverage = 0.885), which dampened Adjusted P3 even further (from 76.8 down to 73.7)."
